<article class="env-definition" id="0GJZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GJZ">Definition <span data-tag="0GJZ">63.12.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a separated scheme of finite type over a field $k$. Let $\Lambda $ be a ring. Let $K$ be an object of $D^+_{tors}(X_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ or of $D(X_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ in case $\Lambda $ is torsion. The <em>cohomology of $K$ with compact support</em> or the <em>compactly supported cohomology of $K$</em> is </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  R\Gamma _ c(X, K) = R\Gamma (\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k), Rf_!K)  \]
</div>
  <p> where $f : X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ is the structure morphism. We will write $H^ i_ c(X, K) = H^ i(R\Gamma _ c(X, K))$. </p>
</article>